## 6. Threat Data & Intelligence

> **Cyber Threat Intelligence (CTI):** The collection, analysis, and dissemination of information regarding active or potential threats, used to drive proactive defense and risk modeling.

### Open-Source Intelligence (OSINT)
Publicly accessible threat data feeds, lists, and advisories:

* **Public & Community-Driven:**
  * [Senki.org](https://www.senki.org/)
  * The MISP Threat Sharing Project
  * AT&T Open Threat Exchange (OTX)
  * [Threatfeeds.io](https://threatfeeds.io/)
* **Government Entities:**
  * Cybersecurity & Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA)
  * DoD Cyber Crime Center (DC3)
  * CISA Automated Indicator Sharing (AIS) program
* **Vendor Feeds & Research:**
  * Microsoft Threat Intelligence
  * Cisco Security Advisories

### Proprietary & Closed-Source Intelligence
Commercial cybersecurity vendors analyze proprietary customer telemetry and internal honeypots:
* Sold as managed feeds, subscription tools, and platform integrations.
* Reduces internal analysis overhead compared to triaging raw OSINT data.
* Often provides visual representations such as real-time **threat maps**.

