## 8. Standards, Protocols, & Sharing

* **STIX (Structured Threat Information eXpression):** A standardized, structured XML/JSON language for describing threat intelligence (tactics, indicators of compromise, threat actors).
* **OpenIOC:** An XML-based framework used to share machine-readable Indicators of Compromise (IoCs).
* **TAXII (Trusted Automated eXchange of Indicator Information):** An application-layer transport protocol communicating over HTTPS to automate the exchange of STIX-formatted intelligence.
* **ISACs (Information Sharing and Analysis Centers):** Sector-specific organizations (e.g., Financial Services, Healthcare, Aviation) facilitating threat intelligence sharing among critical infrastructure stakeholders.

